            "markup": "\u003Ch2\u003EStoolball reports in local newspapers 1747 to 1866\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAndrew Lusted\u2019s second book about stoolball brings together all reports of stoolball from the hundreds of local newspapers held at the British Library. Together the reports paint a picture of a game played by women, children, or both, as an alternative to cricket. With one exception, the game was only played in Sussex at this time.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EIt also includes the first formal rules of stoolball, which were agreed at Glynde in 1867.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe book is just 44 pages with a colour cover and costs \u00A34 (plus \u00A31 postage). Only 100 copies have been printed and they are available from Andrew Lusted at Welsted, Glynde, Lewes BN8 6SU. Cheques should be payable to A Lusted who can be contacted on \u003Ca href=\u0022mailto:lusted.challen@btinternet.com\u0022\u003Elusted.challen@btinternet.com\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        },
